msgid "U575 single-tuple LPTIM1 LPBAM across Stop2"
msgstr "U575 single-tuple LPTIM1 LPBAM across Stop2"

msgid "This reference targets STM32U575ZIT6Q TZEN0 baremetal: one fixed SRAM4 tuple updates LPTIM1 CCR1, RCR and ARR through LPDMA1 channel0 while the same concrete Stop2 owner controls sleep and final release. General LPBAM and the original {download}`IO-32 <io-evolution-execution.csv>` and {download}`SOC-35 <soc-refinement-execution.csv>` exits remain open. Board output routing is unknown; physical HIL is `not_executed`."
msgstr "This reference targets STM32U575ZIT6Q TZEN0 baremetal: one fixed SRAM4 tuple updates LPTIM1 CCR1, RCR and ARR through LPDMA1 channel0 while the same concrete Stop2 owner controls sleep and final release. General LPBAM and the original {download}`IO-32 <io-evolution-execution.csv>` and {download}`SOC-35 <soc-refinement-execution.csv>` exits remain open. Board output routing is unknown; physical HIL is `not_executed`."

msgid "ES0499 section 2.17.3 warns that modifying an interrupt bit in DIER clears its corresponding status flag. Success therefore captures fresh kernel write acknowledgements before producer withdrawal changes DIER. The software model conservatively permits any DIER write to clear all three write-OK flags; this is a defensive test envelope, not a silicon measurement."
msgstr "ES0499 section 2.17.3 warns that modifying an interrupt bit in DIER clears its corresponding status flag. Success therefore captures fresh kernel write acknowledgements before producer withdrawal changes DIER. The software model conservatively permits any DIER write to clear all three write-OK flags; this is a defensive test envelope, not a silicon measurement."

msgid "Link `Nexus::U575Stop2Lptim1`; it brings `Nexus::U575LpdmaLptim1` and retained time. WUT-only, SRAM4-copy and LPTIM1 are mutually exclusive compile-time modes of the same static Stop2 owner and RUN ClockDomain. Default images select none of the new targets. No heap, worker, queue, dynamic MMIO plan, runtime registry or new factory is introduced; vendor types remain private."
msgstr "Link `Nexus::U575Stop2Lptim1`; it brings `Nexus::U575LpdmaLptim1` and retained time. WUT-only, SRAM4-copy and LPTIM1 are mutually exclusive compile-time modes of the same static Stop2 owner and RUN ClockDomain. Default images select none of the new targets. No heap, worker, queue, dynamic MMIO plan, runtime registry or new factory is introduced; vendor types remain private."

