msgid "Prepare the exact owners"
msgstr "Prepare the exact owners"

msgid "Select the maintained [assembly](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/assemblies/u575-lptim1-lpbam-stop2.toml). Its selected SRAM4/LPDMA1 reset startup and the externally prepared LSE RTC provenance remain required. Keep the 16 KiB nonsecure SRAM4 window at `0x28000000..0x28003fff` powered and retained, with SRAM4EN and LPDMA1EN live through every join. Runtime recovery must not rescue lost SRAM4 by changing its power-down fields."
msgstr "Select the maintained [assembly](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/assemblies/u575-lptim1-lpbam-stop2.toml). Its selected SRAM4/LPDMA1 reset startup and the externally prepared LSE RTC provenance remain required. Keep the 16 KiB nonsecure SRAM4 window at `0x28000000..0x28003fff` powered and retained, with SRAM4EN and LPDMA1EN live through every join. Runtime recovery must not rescue lost SRAM4 by changing its power-down fields."

msgid "The existing [retained-clock and Stop2 profile](u575-retained-time.md) requires TZEN0, unswapped Flash, effective MSIS4/MSIK4, equal buses, true Range4 and caches off. All LPDMA channels/vectors start quiet; no other channel may run. The whole LPTIM1 controller is exclusive, initially reset/cold, with its access gate off and kernel mux at reset. No external timer writer, IRQ user or reset may share it. RUN LPTIM2 must already be disabled and joined."
msgstr "The existing [retained-clock and Stop2 profile](u575-retained-time.md) requires TZEN0, unswapped Flash, effective MSIS4/MSIK4, equal buses, true Range4 and caches off. All LPDMA channels/vectors start quiet; no other channel may run. The whole LPTIM1 controller is exclusive, initially reset/cold, with its access gate off and kernel mux at reset. No external timer writer, IRQ user or reset may share it. RUN LPTIM2 must already be disabled and joined."

