msgid "The full tuple and workspace extents must be disjoint SRAM4 spans, separate from request, owner, face, clock, snapshot and other control storage. Callers provide no destination, raw DMA instruction or tuple count. A second tuple would need proof that each preceding asynchronous register write was accepted before reuse; a large ARR cannot bound arbitrary bridge delay. Repetition is outside this API. Host64 receiver storage is 136 B; old copy remains 120 B."
msgstr "The full tuple and workspace extents must be disjoint SRAM4 spans, separate from request, owner, face, clock, snapshot and other control storage. Callers provide no destination, raw DMA instruction or tuple count. A second tuple would need proof that each preceding asynchronous register write was accepted before reuse; a large ARR cannot bound arbitrary bridge delay. Repetition is outside this API. Host64 receiver storage is 136 B; old copy remains 120 B."

msgid "Start, borrow and execute"
msgstr "Start, borrow and execute"

msgid "Initialize ordinary retained time with `wake_owner=nx_stm32u575_stop2_identity()`, then initialize Stop2 and the receiver. No AlarmA-copy initializer is used. Receiver initialization is pure; explicit public `start` prepares access in unmasked privileged Thread."
msgstr "Initialize ordinary retained time with `wake_owner=nx_stm32u575_stop2_identity()`, then initialize Stop2 and the receiver. No AlarmA-copy initializer is used. Receiver initialization is pure; explicit public `start` prepares access in unmasked privileged Thread."

msgid "Start acquires LPTIM1EN, LPTIM1SEL=LSE and only a needed LSESYSEN, observing LSESYSRDY while preserving oscillator/calendar provenance. It writes no timer register. Partial failure retains its ledger and physical reservation; keep storage live and call public `stop` until restoration succeeds. Products need no private RCC preparation writes."
msgstr "Start acquires LPTIM1EN, LPTIM1SEL=LSE and only a needed LSESYSEN, observing LSESYSRDY while preserving oscillator/calendar provenance. It writes no timer register. Partial failure retains its ledger and physical reservation; keep storage live and call public `stop` until restoration succeeds. Products need no private RCC preparation writes."

msgid "Initialize the request base, take a successful retained sample and prepare metadata with the tuple, workspace and an absolute retained-domain deadline or NEVER. Prepare neither borrows nor touches tuple/workspace; keep tuple contents unchanged. Value admission occurs before ACCEPTED. Rejection changes no request byte and retains no new reference; old TIM2 deadlines are never converted."
msgstr "Initialize the request base, take a successful retained sample and prepare metadata with the tuple, workspace and an absolute retained-domain deadline or NEVER. Prepare neither borrows nor touches tuple/workspace; keep tuple contents unchanged. Value admission occurs before ACCEPTED. Rejection changes no request byte and retains no new reference; old TIM2 deadlines are never converted."

msgid "Close and drain the exact RUN barrier, disable/join LPTIM2 and stop Platform. Enter with privileged MSP Thread, CONTROL0, PRIMASK1 and BASEPRI/FAULTMASK0; keep masks and RUN admission closed through recovery. Use 4096..65536 RTC/16 escape ticks and a positive per-phase `poll_limit`. ACCEPTED borrows request, tuple and the full workspace until acquire-observed SETTLED and external observer joins, even if later setup fails."
msgstr "Close and drain the exact RUN barrier, disable/join LPTIM2 and stop Platform. Enter with privileged MSP Thread, CONTROL0, PRIMASK1 and BASEPRI/FAULTMASK0; keep masks and RUN admission closed through recovery. Use 4096..65536 RTC/16 escape ticks and a positive per-phase `poll_limit`. ACCEPTED borrows request, tuple and the full workspace until acquire-observed SETTLED and external observer joins, even if later setup fails."

msgid "After observed CR.ENABLE, a new successful retained sample anchors a bounded wait for at least two additional 256 Hz RTC ticks, checking the request deadline. An arbitrarily short first tick still leaves one full 128-LSE-cycle interval, exceeding two counter cycles. Poll counts alone prove no time. PRELOAD1, one CC1E setup and initial CCR1=0/RCR=0/ARR=1023 require fresh CMP1OK/REPOK/ARROK; those initial flags must then be cleared and observed clear before DMA."
msgstr "After observed CR.ENABLE, a new successful retained sample anchors a bounded wait for at least two additional 256 Hz RTC ticks, checking the request deadline. An arbitrarily short first tick still leaves one full 128-LSE-cycle interval, exceeding two counter cycles. Poll counts alone prove no time. PRELOAD1, one CC1E setup and initial CCR1=0/RCR=0/ARR=1023 require fresh CMP1OK/REPOK/ARROK; those initial flags must then be cleared and observed clear before DMA."

msgid "The first 32-bit CCR1 write waits for request13 `lptim1_ue_dma` with BREQ1, SWREQ0 and reserved DREQ0. Two generated software-requested LLIs write RCR then ARR last, using fixed noncontiguous destinations and no destination increment. ARR's acknowledged APB write clears UE; the final link is zero and completion is at the last LLI. WUT escapes independently; no AlarmA register or GPIO is configured. Success means synchronized register writes, not a full PWM period."
msgstr "The first 32-bit CCR1 write waits for request13 `lptim1_ue_dma` with BREQ1, SWREQ0 and reserved DREQ0. Two generated software-requested LLIs write RCR then ARR last, using fixed noncontiguous destinations and no destination increment. ARR's acknowledged APB write clears UE; the final link is zero and completion is at the last LLI. WUT escapes independently; no AlarmA register or GPIO is configured. Success means synchronized register writes, not a full PWM period."

msgid "Prove success, isolate and join"
msgstr "Prove success, isolate and join"

msgid "Success latches both finite DMA completion and fresh CMP1OK/REPOK/ARROK before UEDE0 or any DIER withdrawal write can clear those flags. A quiet flag after DIER is not that proof. Each admission and completed owned isolation clears the saved proof within the existing 16 B ledger. Error or partial cancellation need no write-OK for unissued writes; master isolation and owned reset can terminate such a request with error."
msgstr "Success latches both finite DMA completion and fresh CMP1OK/REPOK/ARROK before UEDE0 or any DIER withdrawal write can clear those flags. A quiet flag after DIER is not that proof. Each admission and completed owned isolation clears the saved proof within the existing 16 B ledger. Error or partial cancellation need no write-OK for unissued writes; master isolation and owned reset can terminate such a request with error."

msgid "Without a terminal DMA state or prior failure, public `service` returns BUSY and leaves UEDE enabled so the pending hardware request can still occur. A pending IRQ is only a hint. If concrete Stop2 cleanup cannot prove completion, it retains the loan and records an error for explicit recovery."
msgstr "Without a terminal DMA state or prior failure, public `service` returns BUSY and leaves UEDE enabled so the pending hardware request can still occur. A pending IRQ is only a hint. If concrete Stop2 cleanup cannot prove completion, it retains the loan and records an error for explicit recovery."

msgid "After finite DMA completion, an incomplete bounded fresh write-OK proof latches `NX_ERROR_IO` and returns BUSY while retaining producer and loan on that call. The next public `service` or concrete `recover` takes the error drain path even if those flags never arrive. This is failure to prove kernel receipt, not an elapsed deadline inferred from poll counts."
msgstr "After finite DMA completion, an incomplete bounded fresh write-OK proof latches `NX_ERROR_IO` and returns BUSY while retaining producer and loan on that call. The next public `service` or concrete `recover` takes the error drain path even if those flags never arrive. This is failure to prove kernel receipt, not an elapsed deadline inferred from poll counts."

msgid "WUT, deadline, cancel and recovery errors enter the first-failure ledger before producer withdrawal. A TC arriving between that decision and the DIER write may increase the observed transfer prefix; it cannot upgrade the terminal error to success. Public `service` never publishes SETTLED; the same concrete Stop2 owner must complete its final detach."
msgstr "WUT, deadline, cancel and recovery errors enter the first-failure ledger before producer withdrawal. A TC arriving between that decision and the DIER write may increase the observed transfer prefix; it cannot upgrade the terminal error to success. Public `service` never publishes SETTLED; the same concrete Stop2 owner must complete its final detach."

msgid "With a valid access profile, withdraw UEDE and observe fresh DIEROK before another DIER write, then require suspend/SUSPF/idle for an enabled DMA channel or observed idle for an already completed channel. Prove full-word RESET and the entire CCR equal to zero. Clear channel addresses, links, flags and IRQ references before resetting exclusively owned LPTIM1 through RCC. Never clear CR.ENABLE: ES0499 section 2.17.1 requires reset shutdown. Preserve unrelated gates, mux fields and RTC/LSE provenance; owned reset must not erase any external controller state."
msgstr "With a valid access profile, withdraw UEDE and observe fresh DIEROK before another DIER write, then require suspend/SUSPF/idle for an enabled DMA channel or observed idle for an already completed channel. Prove full-word RESET and the entire CCR equal to zero. Clear channel addresses, links, flags and IRQ references before resetting exclusively owned LPTIM1 through RCC. Never clear CR.ENABLE: ES0499 section 2.17.1 requires reset shutdown. Preserve unrelated gates, mux fields and RTC/LSE provenance; owned reset must not erase any external controller state."

msgid "Unknown access profiles permit no RTC/LPTIM/DMA MMIO and retain effects and storage. Concrete Stop2 recovery retries without WFI. Owned reset failure is retryable only after DMA final-access proof; observed external DMA or LPTIM reset during an active loan permanently quarantines it until actual external system reset. Deassertion or quiet reset defaults cannot release that loan."
msgstr "Unknown access profiles permit no RTC/LPTIM/DMA MMIO and retain effects and storage. Concrete Stop2 recovery retries without WFI. Owned reset failure is retryable only after DMA final-access proof; observed external DMA or LPTIM reset during an active loan permanently quarantines it until actual external system reset. Deassertion or quiet reset defaults cannot release that loan."

msgid "Cancel/deadline never revoke storage. Only after peripheral, DMA, IRQ, loan gates, RTC/WUT, power and clock restoration does Stop2 detach references and release-publish SETTLED as its final request access. Public-start claims remain reserved until joined public `stop` restores them, including stop requested during a loan. Reopen RUN and restart Platform only after all effects drain; old Core TIM2 deadlines remain invalid."
msgstr "Cancel/deadline never revoke storage. Only after peripheral, DMA, IRQ, loan gates, RTC/WUT, power and clock restoration does Stop2 detach references and release-publish SETTLED as its final request access. Public-start claims remain reserved until joined public `stop` restores them, including stop requested during a loan. Reopen RUN and restart Platform only after all effects drain; old Core TIM2 deadlines remain invalid."

msgid "Sources and verification boundary"
msgstr "Sources and verification boundary"

msgid "Focused production-C GoogleTest models pass 24 cases in debug and 24 with Os, including conservative DIER flag loss, early service, missing acknowledgements, partial cancellation, late TC and proof reuse. Legacy memory-copy receiver31 and coupled17 cases remain green. A selective strict C11 Cortex-M33 development relink recompiles the receiver and Stop2 units and reuses the pinned startup, public consumer and unchanged dependency libraries. These checks establish no complete SDK or candidate qualification."
msgstr "Focused production-C GoogleTest models pass 24 cases in debug and 24 with Os, including conservative DIER flag loss, early service, missing acknowledgements, partial cancellation, late TC and proof reuse. Legacy memory-copy receiver31 and coupled17 cases remain green. A selective strict C11 Cortex-M33 development relink recompiles the receiver and Stop2 units and reuses the pinned startup, public consumer and unchanged dependency libraries. These checks establish no complete SDK or candidate qualification."

msgid "RM0456 Rev7 anchors are sections 18.3.3/Table148 (request13), 18.3.4/Table149 (BREQ), 18.8.11 (reserved DREQ), 58.4.11/13 (write-OK/enable delay), 58.4.20–21 (CCR1→RCR→ARR/UEDE), 58.5 (LPTIM2 disabled before Stop2), 58.7.8 (DIEROK), and 11.8.48–49 (LSE mux/system gate). ES0499 Rev12 sections 2.17.1–3 govern reset, repeat/APB constraints and DIER flags; RCR0 and LSE≤PCLK exclude the odd-repeat profile. Physical waveform, retention, residency, accuracy, wake and power checks remain `not_executed`; no original IO-32/SOC-35 exit is promoted."
msgstr "RM0456 Rev7 anchors are sections 18.3.3/Table148 (request13), 18.3.4/Table149 (BREQ), 18.8.11 (reserved DREQ), 58.4.11/13 (write-OK/enable delay), 58.4.20–21 (CCR1→RCR→ARR/UEDE), 58.5 (LPTIM2 disabled before Stop2), 58.7.8 (DIEROK), and 11.8.48–49 (LSE mux/system gate). ES0499 Rev12 sections 2.17.1–3 govern reset, repeat/APB constraints and DIER flags; RCR0 and LSE≤PCLK exclude the odd-repeat profile. Physical waveform, retention, residency, accuracy, wake and power checks remain `not_executed`; no original IO-32/SOC-35 exit is promoted."

